#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Makes samples/ace4's Excel 4.0 macro sheets, for tools/samples/gather and PLAN.md 4.7. Nothing here
writes one, so each is written by hand from its format: .xlsm is zipped XML, .xls is BIFF8 records in a
compound file (MS-XLS, MS-CFB), and .xlsb is BIFF12 records in a zip (MS-XLSB). Only the standard library
is used and the bytes are the same on every run.

    make-xlm <out dir>

The URLs are example.com's. Each macro runs HALT() at its end, so none loops except xlm_loop's, whose
WHILE never ends: it's what a pass's 30 s timeout is for.
"""

